# crafty publishing (library-and-publishing)

See [docs/process.md](../../docs/process.md) and [docs/releasing.md](../../docs/releasing.md).

## Never do this on a real release

```bash
cargo publish --workspace   # ❌ bursts new crates → HTTP 429
```

Use **`./scripts/publish-workspace.sh`**.

## Release flow

```bash
# CHANGELOG: move [Unreleased] → new version section
./scripts/release.sh 0.2.0 --publish              # gate + tag + publish + push (default)
./scripts/release.sh 0.2.0 --publish --no-push    # crates.io only
./scripts/release.sh --dry-run                    # release gate only
```

`release.sh --publish` runs release gate (autofix, ci-fast-lane, MSRV strict, release build), pushes git by default.

## crates.io rate limits

Use `publish-workspace.sh` — dependency order, skip indexed, retry 429. Default **30s** between uploads.

## Prerequisites

- `CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN` or `cargo login`
- Clean tree for prepare
- MSRV toolchain for release gate

## CI

- Tag `publish-dry-run`: full `ci-fast-lane.sh`
- Tag manual `publish`: `publish-workspace.sh` + `post-publish-docs.sh`

